   "reason": "Statement labels. `99 close (107)` is not recognised as I/O by a pattern anchored on the keyword, and `10  enddo` is not recognised as a block close, so the loop it ends stays open and swallows the enclosing `end if` -- leaving one construct unclosed tree-wide and every statement after it one level too deep."
